//
// 250 levels of nesting — below `MAX_PARSE_DEPTH` (256) — compile and run on both backends:
// the bound refuses only what the stack cannot hold.  `(1 + (1 + … (1 + 0)))` with 250 ones is
// 250.  Its refused twin is `an-expression-nested-past-the-bound-is-refused.loft`.
//
// @falsified-at: none — it pins the bound's lower side, which no earlier build refused; a
//   bound set below 250 fails it with the refusal.

